# Riven working artifacts (pieces and keys may be sensitive).
#
# Pieces are named "<base>.<serial>" with a per-format suffix, so the numbered
# forms below are what a stray binary piece or word list looks like. The .txt
# (base64) and .png (QR) forms cannot be globbed without swallowing ordinary
# project files, so keep pieces in their own directory rather than relying on
# this. -o/--out is there for that.
*.[0-9]
*.[0-9][0-9]
*.[0-9][0-9][0-9]
*.b32.txt
*.words.txt
*.key
*.pub
scratch/
pieces/
testdata/tmp/

# Go workspace
go.work
go.work.sum

# Lock file created by the build scripts while taking a build number
version/build_number.txt.lock
